columns: gap1 / gap32 = the synthetic top-1 - top-2 / top-32 gaps (compare with the measured medians 12.00 / 18.06); cand = the candidate's logit; cosmax = the largest cosine any row reaches;
global / chnk64 / chk256 = fraction of the vocabulary pruned by ||h|| ||w_v||, by sum over 40 or 10 chunks of ||h_c|| ||w_{v,c}||; box = the code-box bound from scales / biases alone;
prg f = exact partial sum over the first f of the dims + Cauchy-Schwarz on the rest. A pruned row's codes (1,280 B) and scales / biases (160 B) are not read; the 40-chunk norm table costs 80 B per row (20 MB), the 10-chunk one 20 B (5 MB), the box bound reads the 40 MB of scales / biases.
